% A user module carrying a bundled library's name. Compiling it
% alongside a module that writes `use_module(library(lists))` puts two
% modules named `lists` in play: this one, and the embedded library
% pulled in by that import. Module identity is the name alone, so
% keeping both would list two providers for every exported name and make
% each use ambiguous (YCHR-20012). The explicitly supplied module wins.
%
% `length/1` deliberately disagrees with the real `lists:length/1` so the
% goal's result shows which module was used.
:- module(lists, [fun length/1]).

:- function length(list(T)) -> int.

length(_) -> 42.
